":" themes them all. To open an edition from your own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interface instead, such as a button or a list you design, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/FeedReaderViewController"},{"text":"; see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/Presenting-the-Prebuilt-Reader"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"To show every screen at once, in the SDK’s own tabs, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/Setting-Up-the-Carousel"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Embedding a Screen","anchor":"Embedding-a-Screen","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UIKit apps place the screens like any other view controller. In SwiftUI,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrap one in a "},{"code":"UIViewControllerRepresentable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; its coordinator is a good"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"home for delegates that need your app’s state, such as a paywall that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checks the user’s subscription:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"tabs":[{"content":[{"type":"codeListing","showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"code":["let archive = ArchiveViewController(","    globalConfig: globalConfig,","    archiveType: .feedArchive(guid: \"PUBLICATION_GUID\", publicationName: \"The Daily\")",")","navigationController?.pushViewController(archive, animated: true)"],"wrap":0},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each screen fills its view, and your navigation bar and tab bar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stay yours.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"title":"UIKit"},{"title":"SwiftUI","content":[{"type":"codeListing","showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"code":["import PSReader","import SwiftUI","","struct ArchiveView: UIViewControllerRepresentable {","    let isSubscribed: Bool","","    func makeCoordinator() -> Coordinator {","        Coordinator()","    }","","    func makeUIViewController(context: Context) -> ArchiveViewController {","        context.coordinator.isSubscribed = isSubscribed","","        let globalConfig = GlobalConfiguration(","            apiKey: \"API_KEY\",","            accountGUID: \"ACCOUNT_GUID\",","            paywallDelegate: context.coordinator","        )","        return ArchiveViewController(","            globalConfig: globalConfig,","            archiveType: .feedArchive(guid: \"PUBLICATION_GUID\", publicationName: \"The Daily\")","        )","    }","","    func updateUIViewController(_ archive: ArchiveViewController, context: Context) {","        context.coordinator.isSubscribed = isSubscribed","    }","","    final class Coordinator: PaywallDelegate {","        var isSubscribed = false","","        func paywallViewControllerForAction(openFeedEdition published: PSEPublished) -> PaywallViewController? {","            isSubscribed ? nil : SubscribeViewController()","        }","","        func paywallViewControllerForAction(openReplicaEdition edition: PSEdition) -> PaywallViewController? {","            nil","        }","    }","}"],"wrap":0},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SubscribeViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stands for your own paywall screen; see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/Paywalls","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". The same pattern works for any delegate: conform"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the coordinator and pass "},{"code":"context.coordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the matching"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/GlobalConfiguration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"tabNavigator"},{"text":"Setting the App Configuration","anchor":"Setting-the-App-Configuration","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Screens you embed have no dynamic archive to load your app configuration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from PageSuite, and a few reader features read it, in-article adverts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among them. If your editions use them, load the configuration with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/AppConfigService","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and set it on your global configuration before you"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"create the screens, which copy the global configuration when you create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","showLineNumbers":false,"syntax":"swift","copyToClipboard":true,"lineAnnotations":[],"code":["var globalConfig = GlobalConfiguration(apiKey: \"API_KEY\", accountGUID: \"ACCOUNT_GUID\")","globalConfig.remoteConfig = try? await AppConfigService().configuration(forShortcode: \"SHORTCODE\")","","let archive = ArchiveViewController(","    globalConfig: globalConfig,","    archiveType: .feedArchive(guid: \"PUBLICATION_GUID\", publicationName: \"The Daily\")",")"],"wrap":0},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Run it in an async context, such as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" you start when your scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connects, and create the screens once it returns.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/Configuring-the-Prebuilt-UI#The-App-Configuration"},{"text":" lists the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"features that need it; if your editions use none of them, skip this step.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Showing-an-Archive","text":"Showing an Archive"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" shows one publication’s editions in a grid, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"latest edition first and largest. Create it with the publication GUID and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a publication name, which becomes each edition’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/PSEPublished\/publicationName","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","lineAnnotations":[],"showLineNumbers":false,"copyToClipboard":true,"code":["var archiveConfig = ArchiveConfiguration(globalConfig: globalConfig)","archiveConfig.maxContentWidth = 900","archiveConfig.datePicker = ArchiveDatePickerConfiguration(globalConfig: globalConfig)","","let archive = ArchiveViewController(","    globalConfig: globalConfig,","    archiveConfig: archiveConfig,","    archiveType: .feedArchive(guid: \"PUBLICATION_GUID\", publicationName: \"The Daily\")",")"],"wrap":0},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveConfiguration","isActive":true},{"text":" controls the grid: thumbnail shape","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveConfiguration\/cellAspectRatio","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveConfiguration\/thumbnailContentMode","isActive":true},{"text":"), labels, the download","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"button, how many editions to list, and the reader that editions open in.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Two values matter most when you embed the screen:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveConfiguration\/maxContentWidth","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" caps the grid’s width in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"regular-width environment, such as a full-screen iPad, and centers it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Compact widths ignore it."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveConfiguration\/datePicker"},{"text":" adds a month picker above the grid.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The editions for a month come from the backend that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pagesuite.PSReader\/documentation\/PSReader\/ArchiveConfiguration\/feedPublicationType-swift.property"},{"text":" names, which must match the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"publication’s type in PageSuite. The default, ","type":"text"},{"code":".app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", suits most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"publications; ask PageSuite if you’re unsure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"name":"Replica","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":